From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Szabo <szotyesz@Mac.home>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 08:51:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] FEXCore: Shrink the call-ret stack to 256 KB.

Every code invalidation that hits a thread's cached code clears that
thread's call-ret stack with VirtualDontNeed, which on Windows decommits
and recommits all of it. Under Wine on macOS that is a mapping change
over 4 MB, and anti-tamper code that patches its own instructions
(Age of Empires II: Definitive Edition's) invalidates code thousands of
times a second: about half the time of each patch went to it.

256 KB still holds 4096 nested calls below the default position; deeper
call chains overflow into the guard page and reset, as before. A
benchmark of the patch pattern (MacNeutron's wine-arm64/tests/
x64-arxantrap.c) went from 26 to 15 us a patch.

Downstream MacNeutron patch, not for upstream FEX, which does not accept
AI-generated code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Debug/InternalThreadState.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Debug/InternalThreadState.h b/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Debug/InternalThreadState.h
index 42feabb..6193bfd 100644
--- a/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Debug/InternalThreadState.h
+++ b/FEXCore/include/FEXCore/Debug/InternalThreadState.h
@@ -109,7 +109,7 @@ struct alignas(FEXCore::Utils::FEX_PAGE_SIZE) InternalThreadState : public FEXCo
   ///< Data pointer for exclusive use by the frontend
   void* FrontendPtr;
 
-  static constexpr size_t CALLRET_STACK_SIZE {0x400000};
+  static constexpr size_t CALLRET_STACK_SIZE {0x40000};
 
   // The low address of the call-ret stack allocation (not including guard pages)
   void* CallRetStackBase {};
